[{:adr/consequences "{:immediate_fixes \"both defects are fixed and merged/committed; network-isekai's live\\n                     browser execution runs correctly end-to-end with zero Rust; all 18\\n                     kami-genre-base-systems genres are confirmed to actually run, not\\n                     merely appear to be authored correctly\", :standing_process_change \"any future work on kami-engine-clj itself, or on any\\n                             kami-engine-clj-consuming game/genre-system repo, should run\\n                             (or extend) the scripts/verify/-pattern two-stage check before\\n                             claiming a compile-level change is safe -- JVM-only test\\n                             passage is no longer sufficient grounds for that claim in this\\n                             codebase\", :discovery_cost_acknowledged \"this defect class went undetected through this session's\\n                                 entire earlier compiler-authoring and genre-system-building\\n                                 work (multiple forks, ~600K+ tokens each) because the\\n                                 verification methodology itself had this gap -- the fix is\\n                                 cheap (one helper function, one accessor-wrapping pass) but\\n                                 the exposure window was the full session until real\\n                                 browser/WASM execution was finally exercised end-to-end\"}", :adr/authoritative_for ["kotoba.engine-clj's JVM test suite (`clojure -M:test`) passing is NOT sufficient\n    evidence that compiled game logic is correct -- the i64.const 32-bit truncation bug\n    (below) only manifested under ClojureScript's numeric semantics and was invisible to\n    every JVM test this session ran, including the 51/51-green suite that predated and\n    postdated the bug's presence in the codebase" "the standard verification bar for kami-engine-clj-compiled game logic going forward is:\n    compile via the real CLJS/ClojureScript path (not JVM), AND actually instantiate+run\n    the resulting .wasm bytes via a real WASM host (kami-script-runtime-rs's wasmtime/wasmi,\n    or a real browser's WebAssembly.instantiate) -- structural validation\n    (`wasm-tools validate`) alone is also insufficient, since it only confirms well-formed\n    WASM, not semantically-correct WASM" "kotoba-lang/kami-genre-base-systems' `scripts/verify/` (added this session, commit\n    `2c4c092`) implements this two-stage standard (CLJS compile -> kami-host execution) and\n    is the reference implementation other kami-engine-clj-consuming projects should follow" "`author.clj` running successfully (producing a valid scene.edn) proves NOTHING about\n    whether the corresponding `logic.clj` compiles or runs -- these are two entirely\n    separate paths (datalevin->scene.edn vs. logic.clj->codegen->wasm) and this session\n    spent most of its game-development work verifying only the former for\n    kami-genre-base-systems' 18 genres, letting 16/18 real compile failures go undetected\n    until this ADR's investigated section's explicit logic.clj compile sweep"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "kami-engine-clj-wasm-verification", :adr/related ["CLAUDE.md" "90-docs/adr/2607032100-consolidate-engine-into-kami-engine-clj.md" "90-docs/adr/2607032400-network-isekai-primary-consolidation.md" "kotoba-lang/kami-engine PR #95 (fix/cljs-i64-const-32bit-truncation, merged a47f2623)" "gftdcojp/network-isekai issue #49 (closed)" "kotoba-lang/kami-genre-base-systems@cafb82e (16-genre defatom-read fix)" "kotoba-lang/kami-genre-base-systems@2c4c092 (scripts/verify/)"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607032500-wasm-verification-standard", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-03", :adr/decision "{:standard \"kami-engine-clj-compiled game logic is not 'verified' until it has: (1)\\n             compiled through the real CLJS/ClojureScript path (kotoba.engine-clj running\\n             under shadow-cljs or equivalent, not JVM clojure), producing actual .wasm\\n             bytes, and (2) those bytes have been instantiated and actually RUN via a real\\n             WASM host (kami-script-runtime-rs's wasmtime or wasmi, or an actual browser's\\n             WebAssembly.instantiate) for enough ticks to observe genuinely\\n             mechanic-specific behavior, not just absence-of-crash. JVM `codegen/compile`\\n             succeeding, or `author.clj` running, or `wasm-tools validate` passing bytes\\n             structurally, are each individually necessary-but-far-from-sufficient checks\\n             -- useful as fast preliminary filters, never presented or relied on as\\n             confirmation of correctness on their own\", :why_jvm_specifically_insufficient \"Clojure's bitwise operators are full-width 64-bit\\n             `long` operations on the JVM but compile to JavaScript's native 32-bit\\n             bitwise operators under ClojureScript (per the ECMAScript spec's ToInt32/\\n             ToUint32 coercion) -- any kami-engine-clj codegen path that packs/unpacks\\n             values wider than 32 bits via bitwise ops is a live risk of exactly Defect 1's\\n             bug class recurring silently, invisible to the JVM test suite by\\n             construction, not by bad luck\", :why_author_clj_specifically_insufficient \"author.clj only exercises the\\n             datalevin -> Datalog-query -> scene.edn projection (ADR-0036's authoring\\n             path) -- it has zero code-path overlap with logic.clj's\\n             parse -> codegen -> wasm-bytes compilation. A game whose author.clj runs\\n             perfectly can have a logic.clj that has never successfully compiled, as\\n             Defect 2 demonstrated for 16 of 18 genres simultaneously\", :reference_implementation \"kotoba-lang/kami-genre-base-systems' `scripts/verify/`\\n             (deps.edn + shadow-cljs.edn + verify/core.cljs + run-verify.sh) implements\\n             this exact two-stage standard and is the pattern other kami-engine-clj\\n             consumers (gftdcojp/network-isekai's own game additions, any future\\n             kami-app-{game} crates) should replicate rather than reinvent\", :not_wired_to_ci \"the verification script exists and was run manually end-to-end\\n             (18/18 compile, 18/18 execute) during development, but is NOT wired into\\n             GitHub Actions CI -- `gftdcojp`'s org-level GitHub Actions setting remains\\n             disabled (confirmed multiple times this session, most recently against\\n             network-isekai directly), which is outside this session's control and\\n             requires an org admin. This is a known, previously-reported, unresolved\\n             blocker, not a new gap introduced here\"}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"session continuation of ADR-2607032400's network-isekai integration work: the\\n           user asked to raise game quality via a self-paced /loop, which surfaced two\\n           real, previously-undetected defects, then explicitly redirected verification\\n           methodology mid-session: 'jvm じゃなくて kotoba wasm で動いてほしい' (I want it to\\n           run on kotoba-wasm, not JVM)\", :defect_1 {:what \"gftdcojp/network-isekai#49/#72's 'unreproduced' null-byte tag-string bug\", \"symptom\" \"entity tag strings (e.g. \\\"player\\\", \\\"shiro-pico\\\", \\\"ghost\\\") decoded with\\n              a large null-byte prefix before the correct content, when the compiler's\\n              output was actually instantiated+run in a real browser (headless Chromium) --\\n              but a Node.js-only WebAssembly.instantiate test of the same bytes could NOT\\n              reproduce it, creating a false 'inconclusive/unreproducible' status that\\n              stood for one full session iteration\", \"root_cause\" \"kotoba.engine-clj.codegen/emit-str packs a 64-bit string handle as\\n                 `(abs << 32) | len` via bit-shift-left/bit-or. Under ClojureScript these\\n                 compile to JavaScript's native 32-bit bitwise operators, which ToInt32-\\n                 coerce their operand FIRST -- `abs << 32` silently becomes `abs << 0` =\\n                 `abs`, discarding the high bits entirely. Correct on the JVM, where\\n                 Clojure's bitwise ops operate on full 64-bit longs -- this is exactly why\\n                 `clojure -M:test` (51/51 green throughout) never caught it, and why a\\n                 Node.js smoke test that happened to only exercise values within Node's\\n                 own numeric edge cases initially seemed not to reproduce it either (the\\n                 actual repro required the SAME kind of large packed handle a real browser\\n                 execution against real game data naturally produces). Fixing emit-str\\n                 alone exposed an identical second-layer instance of the same bug class in\\n                 wasm_bytes.cljc's sleb128/uleb128 (bit-and/bit-shift-right/\\n                 unsigned-bit-shift-right also truncate to 32 bits under CLJS)\", \"fix\" \"replaced the large-operand bitwise operations with arithmetic (+/*/mod/quot, via\\n          a new `shr7` floored-division helper) in both call sites -- correct on both JVM\\n          and CLJS since JS doubles are exact for these magnitudes (well under 2^53) and\\n          JVM longs are exact regardless. Values that provably stay within 32 bits (the\\n          LEB128 continuation byte itself, masked to [0,127]) keep their existing bitwise\\n          calls unchanged, since those were never the bug\", \"landed\" \"kotoba-lang/kami-engine PR #95, merged a47f2623dfd6c1888c902fccd3f68a0a7ed2a75.\\n             Re-verified via real headless-Chromium execution of both network-isekai's\\n             tanememi and shiro-pico games post-fix: tag strings decode correctly, ghost\\n             entities show real varying positions across multiple spawns\"}, :defect_2 {:what \"16 of kami-genre-base-systems' 18 genre base systems had never actually been\\n          compiled, at all, on any platform, despite every genre's author.clj having run\\n          successfully all session\", \"root_cause\" \"the maturity pass (adding combo counters, win/lose conditions, currency,\\n                 escalating alert levels, etc. to deepen each genre's core loop) read\\n                 `defatom` values via a bare symbol reference (e.g. `(+ combo 1)`), but\\n                 kotoba.engine-clj's codegen requires the explicit `(atom-val name)`\\n                 accessor for reads -- a bare symbol is only a valid codegen target for\\n                 `set-atom!`'s write side. `sports` additionally used `-`/`<` on f32 values\\n                 where the compiler requires the f32-specific `-f`/`<f` operators. Every\\n                 prior verification pass this session ran `author.clj` (the\\n                 datalevin -> scene.edn data-authoring path) and separately, manually\\n                 code-reviewed `logic.clj` against a proven-vocabulary checklist -- neither\\n                 step ever actually invoked `codegen/compile` on the file, so this was a\\n                 pure compile-time error hiding behind two verification methods that both,\\n                 independently, happened not to exercise the actual compile step\", \"fix\" \"wrapped every value-position defatom reference in `(atom-val ...)` across all 16\\n          affected files; fixed sports' float-op operators. Re-verified all 18/18 compile\\n          via `codegen/compile` (JVM first, then per this ADR's methodology correction,\\n          all 18 also re-verified via the real CLJS path + actual wasmtime execution\\n          through kami-script-runtime-rs's kami-host, not just structural validation)\", \"landed\" \"kotoba-lang/kami-genre-base-systems@cafb82e (16-file fix) and @2c4c092\\n             (scripts/verify/, the standing two-stage verification script this ADR\\n             establishes as the reference pattern)\"}}", :adr/alternatives "[{:option \"keep JVM `clojure -M:test` as the sole/primary compiler-correctness gate,\\n            treat CLJS/browser execution as an optional final smoke test\", :rejected_because \"this was literally the status quo that let Defect 1 ship\\n                       undetected through a fully-green 51/51 JVM test suite for as long\\n                       as it existed in the codebase -- demonstrated insufficient by this\\n                       ADR's own investigation, not a hypothetical concern\"} {:option \"treat `wasm-tools validate` (structural byte validity) as sufficient\\n            verification once real .wasm bytes are produced, without requiring actual\\n            execution\", :rejected_because \"Defect 1's corrupted bytes were structurally valid WASM (any 4-byte\\n                       sequence is a structurally valid f32/i64 immediate) -- validation\\n                       cannot distinguish semantically-wrong-but-well-formed bytes from\\n                       correct ones; only actual execution (observing real, mechanic-\\n                       specific behavior) can\"} {:option \"wire scripts/verify/ into GitHub Actions CI now, matching this session's\\n            earlier attempt for the (now-archived) isekai-network repo\", :rejected_because \"`gftdcojp` org-level GitHub Actions remains disabled, confirmed\\n                       multiple times this session against multiple repos in the org --\\n                       not something this session can resolve; the script exists and is\\n                       ready to wire in the moment that org-level blocker clears\"}]", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607032500: JVM verification is insufficient for kami-engine-clj/kami-genre-base-systems -- real WASM execution is the standard"}]